+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016xLZRKTG2Dndmrev4Mcb3e","type":"tool_result","content":"92418\t##### D.110c-0b0 owner-selection design\n92419\t\n92420\tThe bounded owner audit rejects two superficially attractive shortcuts. The\n92421\texisting creator finality key authenticates checkpoint content but has no\n92422\tmonotonic memory: it can sign two same-epoch forks, and every valid older\n92423\tsignature remains valid. Storing a signed \"latest\" value in the room AHE,\n92424\tIndexedDB, invite, checkpoint, registration, journal, snapshot store, or another\n92425\tdatabase on the same rollbackable storage boundary merely moves the replay\n92426\tproblem. The current `@ts-drp/keychain` derives signing keys from caller seed\n92427\tmaterial and exposes signing, not a platform monotonic counter or independently\n92428\tdurable per-room state. Neither construction can be the floor.\n92429\t\n92430\tThe selected owner is therefore an **application/account-held monotonic room\n92431\thead authority** supplied to the product room as an explicit capability. It is\n92432\tnot a built-in checkpoint server, global ledger, consensus service, or new\n92433\tcryptographic proof. The provider may be backed by an authenticated account\n92434\tservice or a platform credential store with real anti-rollback semantics, but\n92435\tthat backing is application policy outside the room's untrusted storage. A\n92436\tplain IndexedDB/localStorage implementation on the same origin does not satisfy\n92437\tthe hostile-storage acceptance. The capability is trusted only for latestness\n92438\tand availability; protocol-v3 remains responsible for authenticating genesis,\n92439\tcreator/profile/signer-set, epoch/anchor lineage, cut/QC, ACL, history,\n92440\tarchive/state/snapshot/manifest, and recovery bytes.\n92441\t\n92442\tThe compared owner families and dispositions are:\n92443\t\n92444\t| Floor owner family                               | Freshness/root property                                                                                                       | Browser and operational property                                                                                             | Disposition                                                                                                                                          |\n92445\t| ------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n92446\t| Creator signing custody alone                    | Authenticates bytes but remembers no maximum epoch; rollback and same-key forks remain valid.                                 | Existing browser-compatible Ed25519 path, but no monotonic durable cell.                                                     | Rejected as insufficient. The creator key remains the checkpoint signer, never the latestness oracle.                                                |\n92447\t| Application/account-held monotonic room-head pin | Caller-authenticated O(1) cell selects one exact current `(objectId, epoch, currentAnchorDigest)` independently of room data. | Async TypeScript capability is browser-feasible; a real account/platform backing is required for hostile-storage resistance. | **Selected.** This is an acknowledged public product/Node contract addition and must pass this high-risk design review before any production edit.   |\n92448\t| Library-selected external checkpoint service     | Could supply a monotonic authenticated pin and brand-new-client bootstrap.                                                    | Adds a service, availability policy, credential protocol, dependency, and migration chosen by ts-drp.                        | Rejected for D.110c-0b0. Phase 7 may bind the application capability to a separately reviewed service, but ts-drp does not silently choose one here. |\n92449\t| Merkle/recursive proof without an external floor | Authenticates lineage or consistency but cannot establish which valid prefix is latest.                                       | Adds proof machinery without closing rollback freshness.                                                                     | Rejected as a floor. It remains orthogonal to the already selected creator checkpoint design.                                                        |\n92450\t\n92451\tThe new public contract is narrow and explicit. Product ownership begins at\n92452\t`CreateV3RoomSessionInput` in `examples/v3-room/src/index.ts`; Node integration\n92453\ttouches creator adoption commit/reopen/activation and the later generalized\n92454\tclose/adoption owners. D.110c-0b0 first plumbs the provider and a copied exact\n92455\texpected room-head only through the existing first-transition product/Node\n92456\tcommit, reopen, and activation path. Protocol-v3 receives that value at the new\n92457\tbounded checkpoint opener only when D.110c-0b1 implements that later consumer;\n92458\tit never receives the provider or its I/O. The 0b0 publishing capability is\n92459\tmandatory for the creator-owned room session that can close/adopt. Any\n92460\tnon-creator session that cold-reopens an advanced room and claims latestness\n92461\tmust also receive an authenticated current pin through the separately reviewed\n92462\tPhase-7 participant/bootstrap contract; absent that input it fails closed and\n92463\tcannot treat local advanced state as current. The provider exposes one\n92464\tper-room authenticated state:\n92465\t\n92466\t```text\n92467\tscope   = (pinnedGenesisAnchorDigest, objectId)\n92468\tstable  = (objectId, epoch, currentAnchorDigest)\n92469\tpending = null | {\n92470\t  previous: stable,\n92471\t  next: (objectId, epoch + 1, nextAnchorDigest)\n92472\t}\n92473\t```\n92474\t\n92475\tThe previous/next tuples plus immutable provider scope already bind the pending\n92476\ttransition; no redundant commitment field exists. The capability supports an\n92477\taccount-side create-scope-if-never-seen operation, one explicitly authorized\n92478\tlegacy migrate-scope operation, exact read, begin-CAS from\n92479\t`{stable, pending:null}` to `{stable, pending}`, and commit-CAS from that exact\n92480\tpending value to `{stable:next, pending:null}`. All inputs and results are\n92481\tcopied, exact-shaped, and fail closed. No method may\n92482\tselect the greatest stored epoch, accept an absent floor, blindly overwrite a\n92483\tconflict, or expose a general arbitrary-value store. At\n92484\tmost one stable tuple and one pending tuple exist per room, so provider state is\n92485\tO(1) with epoch count.\n92486\t\n92487\tThe publication protocol supplies logical atomicity across the independent\n92488\tauthority and room store without pretending that two physical stores share a\n92489\ttransaction:\n92490\t\n92491\t1. Verify the current stable floor equals the genuine active room head and that\n92492\t   no pending value exists.\n92493\t2. Produce, verify, and durably complete the exact next checkpoint/generation,\n92494\t   while leaving the current room head and activation unchanged.\n92495\t3. Install the exact pending advance through provider CAS. From this point no\n92496\t   old or new room generation may activate until the transition resolves.\n92497\t4. CAS the room AHE head from the exact prior head to the already-complete next\n92498\t   generation. An ambiguous CAS is resolved by an authenticated reopen and\n92499\t   exact equality before step 5; it is never guessed.\n92500\t5. Commit the exact pending provider record to the new stable floor. The\n92501\t   confirmed step-4 head equality plus this commit retire the old stable tuple.\n92502\t6. Reopen both owners, require exact equality at the new tuple, and only then\n92503\t   activate/publish the new owner. This is a fresh publication check, not the\n92504\t   first evidence for step-5 retirement. Old control proof retirement remains\n92505\t   separately subject to adoption, rollback, availability, snapshot, and\n92506\t   outbox gates.\n92507\t\n92508\tAfter pending installation there is no rollback-to-old abort path. Recovery\n92509\teither completes the same exact authenticated transition or remains unavailable\n92510\tand fail closed. This makes every crash state deterministic:\n92511\t\n92512\t| Crash observation                                                                             | Required result                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n92513\t| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n92514\t| Old stable floor, no pending, old room head; next generation absent or merely staged/complete | Old head may reopen; unselected next bytes have no authority.                                                                                                                                                 |\n92515\t| Old stable floor, exact pending next, old room head                                           | No activation. Reverify the pending-selected complete next generation, then perform the exact head CAS and pending commit.                                                                                    |\n92516\t| Old stable floor, exact pending next, next room head                                          | No activation until the provider commits that exact pending value; then exact dual-owner equality is required.                                                                                                |\n92517\t| New stable floor, no pending, next room head                                                  | Reverify checkpoint contents and exact floor equality, then activate.                                                                                                                                         |\n92518\t| Floor behind an authenticated room head with no matching pending                              | `D110C_FLOOR_HEAD_AHEAD`; do not accept the floor-matching old generation and do not synthesize a pending value.                                                                                              |\n92519\t| Floor ahead of room head with no pending                                                      | `D110C_FLOOR_MISMATCH`; never fall back to the largest local epoch or an older matching generation.                                                                                                           |\n92520\t| Malformed/foreign pending, missing selected generation, or unavailable provider               | Typed availability/authority failure; never fall back to the largest local epoch or an older matching generation.                                                                                             |\n92521\t| Two concurrent next heads or a changed provider value                                         | Exact CAS conflict `D110C_FLOOR_CONFLICT`; the losing publication attempt cannot activate. A later reopen observing the exact winning `pending.next` follows pending recovery rather than retrying begin-CAS. |\n92522\t\n92523\tThe focused contract freezes the complete classification set rather than a\n92524\tprefix wildcard:\n92525\t\n92526\t| Condition                                                                 | Exact code                         |\n92527\t| ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n92528\t| Provider create/migrate/read/begin/commit unavailable or throws           | `D110C_FLOOR_UNAVAILABLE`          |\n92529\t| Provider value is malformed, cross-object, cross-genesis, or noncanonical | `D110C_FLOOR_INVALID`              |\n92530\t| Stable floor differs from the sole proposed current authenticated head    | `D110C_FLOOR_MISMATCH`             |\n92531\t| Proposed next epoch/anchor regresses, skips, or reuses the stable tuple   | `D110C_FLOOR_REGRESSION`           |\n92532\t| Exact create/migrate/begin/commit CAS loses or observes another value     | `D110C_FLOOR_CONFLICT`             |\n92533\t| Pending previous/next tuple is missing, duplicate, or inconsistent        | `D110C_FLOOR_PENDING_INVALID`      |\n92534\t| Authenticated room head is ahead while no exact pending advance exists    | `D110C_FLOOR_HEAD_AHEAD`           |\n92535\t| Exact pending-selected complete generation is absent or unavailable       | `D110C_FLOOR_RECOVERY_UNAVAILABLE` |\n92536\t| Any ordinary reopen has no independently authenticated provider scope     | `D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED`   |\n92537\t\n92538\tWhen an exact pending value selects the observed old or next room head, the\n92539\tpending-recovery rows dominate ordinary mismatch classification.\n92540\t`D110C_FLOOR_MISMATCH` applies when the floor is ahead or otherwise differs\n92541\twithout an exact pending selector; `D110C_FLOOR_HEAD_AHEAD` is reserved for an\n92542\tauthenticated room head ahead of the stable floor with no exact pending.\n92543\t\n92544\tCrash completion reads the next tuple from the independently authenticated\n92545\tpending provider record. It may load hostile room bytes only as candidates and\n92546\tmust fully authenticate the candidate against that tuple and the prior trust;\n92547\tit may not derive, repair, or advance the provider value from a local AHE head,\n92548\tcheckpoint, journal, snapshot, invite, or maximum epoch. A provider outage is\n92549\tan availability failure, not permission to weaken freshness. A provider that\n92550\tlies, rolls back, or equivocates is outside the selected trust assumption and\n92551\tcan defeat latestness; this limitation is explicit.\n92552\t\n92553\tInitialization and compatibility are also exact. Only an explicit account-side\n92554\t**new-room creation act** may create a previously unseen provider scope, using\n92555\tcreate-if-never-seen CAS to install\n92556\t`(objectId, 0, pinnedGenesisAnchorDigest)`. It runs as part of new room creation,\n92557\tnot ordinary reopen, and concurrent creators converge only on the identical\n92558\tdeterministic genesis tuple. The provider must remember that the scope has ever\n92559\texisted; erasing the room store or provider value cannot make the scope new\n92560\tagain. If new-room creation aborts after scope creation, the scope remains\n92561\treserved and reopen fails unavailable until the exact genesis room data is\n92562\trestored.\n92563\t\n92564\tOrdinary reopen with an absent provider scope always returns\n92565\t`D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED`, even when hostile local bytes present an\n92566\tauthentic epoch-0 trust root. No local epoch, invite, checkpoint, or signature\n92567\tmay distinguish a legacy unadvanced room from an advanced room rolled back to\n92568\tgenesis. A legacy room may continue only through the explicit one-time\n92569\tmigrate-scope operation using an independently authenticated application/account\n92570\tpin; migration never derives the pin from local room storage. A brand-new client\n92571\twith only genesis can authenticate a checkpoint but cannot establish freshness;\n92572\tPhase 7 must define how its application/account obtains the current pin.\n92573\tStep-4 authenticated head equality authorizes the step-5 provider commit that\n92574\tretires the old stable tuple; step 6 reconfirms equality before publication. No\n92575\ttransition history is retained. D.110c does not implement permanent provider\n92576\tscope deletion: the account authority must retain the last active pin or an\n92577\tO(1) terminal used-scope/tombstone marker. Any erasing deletion policy is a\n92578\tseparate high-risk Phase-7 decision and may never enable create-scope reuse.\n92579\t\n92580\tD.110c-0b0 RED/GREEN is frozen accordingly. RED uses the real first transition\n92581\tand production reopen path to demonstrate all of the following without a\n92582\ttests-only trust record: a valid old generation is accepted when no independent\n92583\tfloor exists; a creator signature alone cannot distinguish latestness; and the\n92584\tcurrent APIs have no provider/pending/CAS seam. GREEN adds only the reviewed\n92585\tcapability/public-contract boundary and the first-transition orchestration. It\n92586\tmust prove:\n92587\t\n92588\t- exact account-side create-if-never-seen genesis initialization, exact\n92589\t  current-head equality, and refusal to initialize during ordinary reopen;\n92590\t- make-before-publish ordering and no activation during a pending transition;\n92591\t- every crash row above in both before/after orderings, including ambiguous\n92592\t  room-head CAS recovery;\n92593\t- stale, forked, skipped, duplicate, cross-object, cross-genesis, regressed,\n92594\t  malformed, missing, unavailable, and concurrent-provider mutants fail with\n92595\t  exact `D110C_FLOOR_*` codes before activation or deletion;\n92596\t- neither normal nor crash recovery derives the provider value from hostile\n92597\t  local data;\n92598\t- creator-owned close/adopt sessions require the publishing capability;\n92599\t  participant advanced reopen without a separately authenticated Phase-7 pin\n92600\t  fails closed and is not silently treated as creator-floor custody;\n92601\t- the provider contains exactly one stable and at most one pending fixed-size\n92602\t  record, old values retire only after step-4 authenticated head equality plus\n92603\t  the exact step-5 commit, step 6 gates publication, and the D.110c-c/d censuses\n92604\t  count it;\n92605\t- fresh account-side epoch-0 creation succeeds; every ordinary reopen with a\n92606\t  missing scope, including local epoch 0, returns\n92607\t  `D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED`; explicit migration requires an\n92608\t  independently authenticated pin; used scopes cannot be re-created; and no\n92609\t  silent migration occurs;\n92610\t  and\n92611\t- the existing wire records, anchor/QC semantics, creator key, thresholds,\n92612\t  dependencies, room workload, and storage schemas remain unchanged.\n92613\t\n92614\tThe retained transition is explicit rather than contradictory. Creator-owned\n92615\tPhase-6a adoption/reopen cases receive the deterministic model implementation\n92616\tof the new account capability and must retain their existing semantic success.\n92617\tThe established-peer and fresh-late-peer cold-reopen cases in\n92618\t`packages/storage-browser/tests/phase-6a-creator-successor-product.pw.ts`, and\n92619\tthe cold activation/reopen cases in\n92620\t`tests/phase-6a-creator-successor-activation-red.test.ts`, become exact 0b0 RED\n92621\twhen no independently authenticated pin is supplied: they fail before room\n92622\tauthority or activation with `D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED` or the named\n92623\tavailability owner. Their original success remains retained only in the paired\n92624\tcase that supplies a separately authenticated application/account test pin.\n92625\tThis changes no D.108 evidence retrospectively; it freezes how those same\n92626\tgolden-path controls are interpreted after the new mandatory freshness owner\n92627\texists.\n92628\t\n92629\tFocused gates cover a deterministic in-memory hostile room store and a separate\n92630\tmodel provider, real browser room reopen with an injected account-authority\n92631\ttest implementation, creator trust/close/adoption retained vectors, exact\n92632\tpublic source shape, package builds/typechecks, exact-owner lint/format/diff,\n92633\tprotected paths/stashes, and signed/pushed evidence. The browser test provider\n92634\tis an implementation of the public authority contract, not evidence that\n92635\tIndexedDB itself is anti-rollback. If production implementation requires a new\n92636\tprotocol wire/schema field, cryptographic dependency, built-in external\n92637\tservice, keychain mutation/counter, changed genesis assumption, or any public\n92638\tsurface broader than this exact capability and expected-head plumbing, stop\n92639\tand reslice before production edits. After reviewed 0b0 GREEN, D.110c-a/b must\n92640\tgeneralize the identical protocol to every genuine transition; 0b1 consumes the\n92641\tstable exact floor for bounded cold trust opening; D.110c-c/d prove retirement,\n92642\trestart, census, and at least 100 transitions; Phase 7 owns new-client pin\n92643\tdistribution and archive/cold-join availability.\n92644\t\n92645\tThe D.110c-0b0 executable RED is now frozen without reopening the accepted\n92646\towner-selection design. Its sole new owner is\n92647\t`tests/phase-6b-d110c-0b0-floor-red.test.ts`, initial SHA-256\n92648\t`d9b41102189c0bf3e703d026ed050e08fc395f1dd815101ec9d6975c49258252`.\n92649\tThe test creates the genuine D.108 first-transition fixture, durably commits the\n92650\tepoch-1 successor, transfers the resulting exact durable carriers to the\n92651\texisting fresh-process production cold-reopen child, and supplies no\n92652\tindependent room-head authority. The current implementation activates that\n92653\tadvanced room, so the exact expected RED failure token is\n92654\t`D110C_0B0_FRESHNESS_FLOOR_MISSING`. GREEN is causal only when the same path\n92655\tinstead returns `{ ok:false, kind:\"D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED\" }` before\n92656\tactivation and the exact reviewed public/provider plumbing is present. Partial,\n92657\tsource-only, fixture-authored, or locally inferred floor evidence cannot satisfy\n92658\tthe test.\n92659\t\n92660\tThe focused RED command is exactly\n92661\t`pnpm exec vitest run tests/phase-6b-d110c-0b0-floor-red.test.ts\n92662\t--reporter=json --outputFile=.logs/d110c-0b0-red/vitest.json`; it selects one\n92663\ttest in one file and may run once from the signed/pushed freeze checkpoint. Its\n92664\tfresh evidence root records command/stdout/stderr/status, selected/result/error\n92665\tcounts, exact terminal token, source and built-import identities, changed paths,\n92666\tprotected state, and a self-excluding manifest. Before RED, affected workspace\n92667\tpackages are freshly built so the child cannot consume stale `dist` state.\n92668\tRED changes no production source. Starting production SHA-256 values are\n92669\t`be0fae5e22476ebfcf2602c34213df60df954b51f1f2e945807c04a3e7fbb612`\n92670\tfor `examples/v3-room/src/index.ts`,\n92671\t`70dba504e7f71fd830b89f28cbfde0d58a9f51584ca256a6058045e693c6cf46`\n92672\tfor `packages/node/src/creator-adoption-activate.ts`, and\n92673\t`a5fd0c18292e63a8c3f16a2517dff474e7f51c99bf122360a65b87f0c7516db9`\n92674\tfor `packages/node/src/creator-adoption-commit.ts`; lockfile and root-manifest\n92675\tSHA-256 values are\n92676\t`73c7c0660fa32c7380d0fe5a026897a7ad85a40edf1f169730c2d8e44e613a99`\n92677\tand `1baa6c3967e63f1d8af5f1e70c6b6c62e032a90e770f18dd3d86f5cfc40e1a55`.\n92678\tThe already accepted Grok/Kimi/Opus owner-selection plan and confirmation are\n92679\tthe bounded plan review for this executable sub-slice; deterministic RED needs\n92680\tno additional model round. No browser campaign or D.110a invocation is\n92681\tauthorized.\n92682\t\n92683\tThat RED ran exactly once from signed/pushed freeze commit\n92684\t`2ba2752ff5dca0d39656f97b429fe6439be7bae9`, tree\n92685\t`8f77c0b7b5403d411cf9844a01b0f8df7b47a3f8`, after the complete workspace\n92686\tpackage build exited zero with empty stderr. From `2026-09-02T06:04:47Z`\n92687\tthrough `2026-09-02T06:04:54Z`, the exact command selected one test in one\n92688\ttest-result file, returned status 1, and reported zero passes, one failure, zero\n92689\tskips, and no top-level or child-launch error. The genuine freshly built\n92690\tepoch-1 cold reopen activated without any independently authenticated\n92691\troom-head authority; the sole failure was exactly\n92692\t`TypeError: D110C_0B0_FRESHNESS_FLOOR_MISSING`. This is the frozen causal RED:\n92693\tthe creator signature and authentic local successor bytes establish content\n92694\tauthenticity but not freshness.\n92695\t\n92696\tThe accepted RED audit SHA-256 is\n92697\t`834e8c20a85a6d1a74cd28a51b4832c1645e6005263c505f9556a763c593306a`.\n92698\tIt proves local/upstream equality at the freeze commit, exact freshly built\n92699\tpackage import ownership, unchanged production/lockfile identities, zero\n92700\ttracked dirt before evidence recording, 26 preserved stashes, all protected\n92701\troots present, no relevant ts-drp process, all four fixed ports clear, and zero\n92702\tcampaign or D.110a invocation. Vitest JSON/stdout/stderr SHA-256 values are\n92703\t`732c82ff6233209326c337cee5f5b3cb50a1b634f0a99609a69a4de931b4e6b5`,\n92704\t`a4dd8d50187eb4056245d66dc1ef35874a59aab64806aad3ed48381b4fd8565d`,\n92705\tand `702197514be5b0d6cfb028f66fe2a1fe0a7cd881be4dafe4ef8e5db2539a5a3f`.\n92706\tThe validating self-excluding RED manifest SHA-256 is\n92707\t`67f6311573e754a3cbd5d4233bd292aee994d06e7b7fbfc674c23b148b639fe2`.\n92708\tThe RED gate is closed and the next authorized state is the narrow D.110c-0b0\n92709\tGREEN; the RED command may not be rerun.\n92710\t\n92711\tThe expressly authorized one-off Fable 5.1/high parallel audit, session\n92712\t`5d9b90ff-5bca-4284-92fa-a9f1018273ff`, independently re-fetched the three\n92713\tpinned Hiero heads, inspected the local trust/closure/reopen owners read-only,\n92714\tand returned `P0=0/P1=0`. It agrees that WRAPS is unnecessary for the fixed\n92715\tcreator signer and cannot supply freshness, and that deterministic provider\n92716\ttests prove correctness assuming an honest external authority rather than\n92717\tbrowser-only rollback resistance. Therefore D.110c-c/d and Phase 7 may claim\n92718\thostile-storage freshness only when a real application/account provider exists\n92719\toutside that storage boundary. Its preferred simpler caller-held-genesis-carrier\n92720\tvariant and its QC/abort/census observations are P2 design guidance for the\n92721\talready required D.110c-0b1 private-opener stop-check; they do not reopen the\n92722\taccepted architecture or authorize a new record/API/dependency. The durable\n92723\treport SHA-256 is\n92724\t`a9ce81a546d04c282276629e927b04583a44d49d8986efca194f8d2a58fe9ba4`;\n92725\tthe raw local session JSONL SHA-256 is\n92726\t`8d4c6cf06f435a814fe1b59cc9d7fec048006811edf37d573590668e1b19219d`.\n92727\tNo further Fable run is authorized by this result.\n92728\t\n92729\tA second expressly authorized one-off Fable 5.1/high audit, session\n92730\t`924afa1f-908c-4590-95ba-ce5cfc94f8bc`, completed read-only against RED\n92731\tevidence HEAD `685611728ecfe37bbdb09369f245f9a909fcf776` and the in-progress uncommitted\n92732\t0b0 plumbing. It independently revalidated the same three upstream heads and\n92733\tagain selects the existing creator-signed bounded checkpoint plus the 0b0\n92734\texternal freshness floor; WRAPS is disproportionate for a fixed signer and\n92735\tdoes not establish latestness. It returned no P0. Its three P1 design cautions\n92736\tare accepted prospectively: D.110c-0b1 must declare the genuinely required\n92737\tepoch-N opener/Node-reopen public compatibility boundary before RED; bounded\n92738\tcold reopen authenticates the creator-signed current history root/size rather\n92739\tthan replay-proving every retired historical extension; and retaining the\n92740\timmediate predecessor QC is an explicit fail-closed availability trade rather\n92741\tthan an additional trust root. These cautions do not reopen 0b0, authorize an\n92742\topener change, weaken archive accounting, or claim that a self-authenticating\n92743\tcheckpoint is fresh. The durable report is\n92744\t`.logs/d110c-0b-hiero-fable-924afa1f/report.md`, SHA-256\n92745\t`f9342a7337c1769c4c37d17b7d063acf04cd852ef4abae4b6903affb7f166efd`;\n92746\tthe raw local session JSONL SHA-256 is\n92747\t`9db8635826759afa527d1370cdfbd5df0da63a351c92463ad8a21250ff81be94`.\n92748\tNo further Fable run is authorized by this second result.\n92749\t\n92750\t##### D.110c-0b0a staged adoption and pending-recovery prerequisite\n92751\t\n92752\tThe first 0b0 GREEN composition audit found a narrower prerequisite that the\n92753\taccepted owner design did not make executable. At RED evidence HEAD\n92754\t`685611728ecfe37bbdb09369f245f9a909fcf776`, the exported\n92755\t`commitCreatorSuccessorAdoption()` consumes its one-use authenticated intent,\n92756\tstages/completes the candidate generation, and swaps the AHE head in the same\n92757\tcall. It cannot expose the required durable-complete-but-not-published state in"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b68b30f-133f-4078-a9a7-ee7aeeec8953","uuid":"5437f2fe-407e-4fd0-9736-296ebe5e6476","timestamp":"2026-09-02T08:25:25.587Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/aristotle/Documents/Projects/ts-drp-1/docs/production-hardening/production-hardening-tdd-plan-v2.md","content":"##### D.110c-0b0 owner-selection design\n\nThe bounded owner audit rejects two superficially attractive shortcuts. The\nexisting creator finality key authenticates checkpoint content but has no\nmonotonic memory: it can sign two same-epoch forks, and every valid older\nsignature remains valid. Storing a signed \"latest\" value in the room AHE,\nIndexedDB, invite, checkpoint, registration, journal, snapshot store, or another\ndatabase on the same rollbackable storage boundary merely moves the replay\nproblem. The current `@ts-drp/keychain` derives signing keys from caller seed\nmaterial and exposes signing, not a platform monotonic counter or independently\ndurable per-room state. Neither construction can be the floor.\n\nThe selected owner is therefore an **application/account-held monotonic room\nhead authority** supplied to the product room as an explicit capability. It is\nnot a built-in checkpoint server, global ledger, consensus service, or new\ncryptographic proof. The provider may be backed by an authenticated account\nservice or a platform credential store with real anti-rollback semantics, but\nthat backing is application policy outside the room's untrusted storage. A\nplain IndexedDB/localStorage implementation on the same origin does not satisfy\nthe hostile-storage acceptance. The capability is trusted only for latestness\nand availability; protocol-v3 remains responsible for authenticating genesis,\ncreator/profile/signer-set, epoch/anchor lineage, cut/QC, ACL, history,\narchive/state/snapshot/manifest, and recovery bytes.\n\nThe compared owner families and dispositions are:\n\n| Floor owner family                               | Freshness/root property                                                                                                       | Browser and operational property                                                                                             | Disposition                                                                                                                                          |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Creator signing custody alone                    | Authenticates bytes but remembers no maximum epoch; rollback and same-key forks remain valid.                                 | Existing browser-compatible Ed25519 path, but no monotonic durable cell.                                                     | Rejected as insufficient. The creator key remains the checkpoint signer, never the latestness oracle.                                                |\n| Application/account-held monotonic room-head pin | Caller-authenticated O(1) cell selects one exact current `(objectId, epoch, currentAnchorDigest)` independently of room data. | Async TypeScript capability is browser-feasible; a real account/platform backing is required for hostile-storage resistance. | **Selected.** This is an acknowledged public product/Node contract addition and must pass this high-risk design review before any production edit.   |\n| Library-selected external checkpoint service     | Could supply a monotonic authenticated pin and brand-new-client bootstrap.                                                    | Adds a service, availability policy, credential protocol, dependency, and migration chosen by ts-drp.                        | Rejected for D.110c-0b0. Phase 7 may bind the application capability to a separately reviewed service, but ts-drp does not silently choose one here. |\n| Merkle/recursive proof without an external floor | Authenticates lineage or consistency but cannot establish which valid prefix is latest.                                       | Adds proof machinery without closing rollback freshness.                                                                     | Rejected as a floor. It remains orthogonal to the already selected creator checkpoint design.                                                        |\n\nThe new public contract is narrow and explicit. Product ownership begins at\n`CreateV3RoomSessionInput` in `examples/v3-room/src/index.ts`; Node integration\ntouches creator adoption commit/reopen/activation and the later generalized\nclose/adoption owners. D.110c-0b0 first plumbs the provider and a copied exact\nexpected room-head only through the existing first-transition product/Node\ncommit, reopen, and activation path. Protocol-v3 receives that value at the new\nbounded checkpoint opener only when D.110c-0b1 implements that later consumer;\nit never receives the provider or its I/O. The 0b0 publishing capability is\nmandatory for the creator-owned room session that can close/adopt. Any\nnon-creator session that cold-reopens an advanced room and claims latestness\nmust also receive an authenticated current pin through the separately reviewed\nPhase-7 participant/bootstrap contract; absent that input it fails closed and\ncannot treat local advanced state as current. The provider exposes one\nper-room authenticated state:\n\n```text\nscope   = (pinnedGenesisAnchorDigest, objectId)\nstable  = (objectId, epoch, currentAnchorDigest)\npending = null | {\n  previous: stable,\n  next: (objectId, epoch + 1, nextAnchorDigest)\n}\n```\n\nThe previous/next tuples plus immutable provider scope already bind the pending\ntransition; no redundant commitment field exists. The capability supports an\naccount-side create-scope-if-never-seen operation, one explicitly authorized\nlegacy migrate-scope operation, exact read, begin-CAS from\n`{stable, pending:null}` to `{stable, pending}`, and commit-CAS from that exact\npending value to `{stable:next, pending:null}`. All inputs and results are\ncopied, exact-shaped, and fail closed. No method may\nselect the greatest stored epoch, accept an absent floor, blindly overwrite a\nconflict, or expose a general arbitrary-value store. At\nmost one stable tuple and one pending tuple exist per room, so provider state is\nO(1) with epoch count.\n\nThe publication protocol supplies logical atomicity across the independent\nauthority and room store without pretending that two physical stores share a\ntransaction:\n\n1. Verify the current stable floor equals the genuine active room head and that\n   no pending value exists.\n2. Produce, verify, and durably complete the exact next checkpoint/generation,\n   while leaving the current room head and activation unchanged.\n3. Install the exact pending advance through provider CAS. From this point no\n   old or new room generation may activate until the transition resolves.\n4. CAS the room AHE head from the exact prior head to the already-complete next\n   generation. An ambiguous CAS is resolved by an authenticated reopen and\n   exact equality before step 5; it is never guessed.\n5. Commit the exact pending provider record to the new stable floor. The\n   confirmed step-4 head equality plus this commit retire the old stable tuple.\n6. Reopen both owners, require exact equality at the new tuple, and only then\n   activate/publish the new owner. This is a fresh publication check, not the\n   first evidence for step-5 retirement. Old control proof retirement remains\n   separately subject to adoption, rollback, availability, snapshot, and\n   outbox gates.\n\nAfter pending installation there is no rollback-to-old abort path. Recovery\neither completes the same exact authenticated transition or remains unavailable\nand fail closed. This makes every crash state deterministic:\n\n| Crash observation                                                                             | Required result                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Old stable floor, no pending, old room head; next generation absent or merely staged/complete | Old head may reopen; unselected next bytes have no authority.                                                                                                                                                 |\n| Old stable floor, exact pending next, old room head                                           | No activation. Reverify the pending-selected complete next generation, then perform the exact head CAS and pending commit.                                                                                    |\n| Old stable floor, exact pending next, next room head                                          | No activation until the provider commits that exact pending value; then exact dual-owner equality is required.                                                                                                |\n| New stable floor, no pending, next room head                                                  | Reverify checkpoint contents and exact floor equality, then activate.                                                                                                                                         |\n| Floor behind an authenticated room head with no matching pending                              | `D110C_FLOOR_HEAD_AHEAD`; do not accept the floor-matching old generation and do not synthesize a pending value.                                                                                              |\n| Floor ahead of room head with no pending                                                      | `D110C_FLOOR_MISMATCH`; never fall back to the largest local epoch or an older matching generation.                                                                                                           |\n| Malformed/foreign pending, missing selected generation, or unavailable provider               | Typed availability/authority failure; never fall back to the largest local epoch or an older matching generation.                                                                                             |\n| Two concurrent next heads or a changed provider value                                         | Exact CAS conflict `D110C_FLOOR_CONFLICT`; the losing publication attempt cannot activate. A later reopen observing the exact winning `pending.next` follows pending recovery rather than retrying begin-CAS. |\n\nThe focused contract freezes the complete classification set rather than a\nprefix wildcard:\n\n| Condition                                                                 | Exact code                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| Provider create/migrate/read/begin/commit unavailable or throws           | `D110C_FLOOR_UNAVAILABLE`          |\n| Provider value is malformed, cross-object, cross-genesis, or noncanonical | `D110C_FLOOR_INVALID`              |\n| Stable floor differs from the sole proposed current authenticated head    | `D110C_FLOOR_MISMATCH`             |\n| Proposed next epoch/anchor regresses, skips, or reuses the stable tuple   | `D110C_FLOOR_REGRESSION`           |\n| Exact create/migrate/begin/commit CAS loses or observes another value     | `D110C_FLOOR_CONFLICT`             |\n| Pending previous/next tuple is missing, duplicate, or inconsistent        | `D110C_FLOOR_PENDING_INVALID`      |\n| Authenticated room head is ahead while no exact pending advance exists    | `D110C_FLOOR_HEAD_AHEAD`           |\n| Exact pending-selected complete generation is absent or unavailable       | `D110C_FLOOR_RECOVERY_UNAVAILABLE` |\n| Any ordinary reopen has no independently authenticated provider scope     | `D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED`   |\n\nWhen an exact pending value selects the observed old or next room head, the\npending-recovery rows dominate ordinary mismatch classification.\n`D110C_FLOOR_MISMATCH` applies when the floor is ahead or otherwise differs\nwithout an exact pending selector; `D110C_FLOOR_HEAD_AHEAD` is reserved for an\nauthenticated room head ahead of the stable floor with no exact pending.\n\nCrash completion reads the next tuple from the independently authenticated\npending provider record. It may load hostile room bytes only as candidates and\nmust fully authenticate the candidate against that tuple and the prior trust;\nit may not derive, repair, or advance the provider value from a local AHE head,\ncheckpoint, journal, snapshot, invite, or maximum epoch. A provider outage is\nan availability failure, not permission to weaken freshness. A provider that\nlies, rolls back, or equivocates is outside the selected trust assumption and\ncan defeat latestness; this limitation is explicit.\n\nInitialization and compatibility are also exact. Only an explicit account-side\n**new-room creation act** may create a previously unseen provider scope, using\ncreate-if-never-seen CAS to install\n`(objectId, 0, pinnedGenesisAnchorDigest)`. It runs as part of new room creation,\nnot ordinary reopen, and concurrent creators converge only on the identical\ndeterministic genesis tuple. The provider must remember that the scope has ever\nexisted; erasing the room store or provider value cannot make the scope new\nagain. If new-room creation aborts after scope creation, the scope remains\nreserved and reopen fails unavailable until the exact genesis room data is\nrestored.\n\nOrdinary reopen with an absent provider scope always returns\n`D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED`, even when hostile local bytes present an\nauthentic epoch-0 trust root. No local epoch, invite, checkpoint, or signature\nmay distinguish a legacy unadvanced room from an advanced room rolled back to\ngenesis. A legacy room may continue only through the explicit one-time\nmigrate-scope operation using an independently authenticated application/account\npin; migration never derives the pin from local room storage. A brand-new client\nwith only genesis can authenticate a checkpoint but cannot establish freshness;\nPhase 7 must define how its application/account obtains the current pin.\nStep-4 authenticated head equality authorizes the step-5 provider commit that\nretires the old stable tuple; step 6 reconfirms equality before publication. No\ntransition history is retained. D.110c does not implement permanent provider\nscope deletion: the account authority must retain the last active pin or an\nO(1) terminal used-scope/tombstone marker. Any erasing deletion policy is a\nseparate high-risk Phase-7 decision and may never enable create-scope reuse.\n\nD.110c-0b0 RED/GREEN is frozen accordingly. RED uses the real first transition\nand production reopen path to demonstrate all of the following without a\ntests-only trust record: a valid old generation is accepted when no independent\nfloor exists; a creator signature alone cannot distinguish latestness; and the\ncurrent APIs have no provider/pending/CAS seam. GREEN adds only the reviewed\ncapability/public-contract boundary and the first-transition orchestration. It\nmust prove:\n\n- exact account-side create-if-never-seen genesis initialization, exact\n  current-head equality, and refusal to initialize during ordinary reopen;\n- make-before-publish ordering and no activation during a pending transition;\n- every crash row above in both before/after orderings, including ambiguous\n  room-head CAS recovery;\n- stale, forked, skipped, duplicate, cross-object, cross-genesis, regressed,\n  malformed, missing, unavailable, and concurrent-provider mutants fail with\n  exact `D110C_FLOOR_*` codes before activation or deletion;\n- neither normal nor crash recovery derives the provider value from hostile\n  local data;\n- creator-owned close/adopt sessions require the publishing capability;\n  participant advanced reopen without a separately authenticated Phase-7 pin\n  fails closed and is not silently treated as creator-floor custody;\n- the provider contains exactly one stable and at most one pending fixed-size\n  record, old values retire only after step-4 authenticated head equality plus\n  the exact step-5 commit, step 6 gates publication, and the D.110c-c/d censuses\n  count it;\n- fresh account-side epoch-0 creation succeeds; every ordinary reopen with a\n  missing scope, including local epoch 0, returns\n  `D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED`; explicit migration requires an\n  independently authenticated pin; used scopes cannot be re-created; and no\n  silent migration occurs;\n  and\n- the existing wire records, anchor/QC semantics, creator key, thresholds,\n  dependencies, room workload, and storage schemas remain unchanged.\n\nThe retained transition is explicit rather than contradictory. Creator-owned\nPhase-6a adoption/reopen cases receive the deterministic model implementation\nof the new account capability and must retain their existing semantic success.\nThe established-peer and fresh-late-peer cold-reopen cases in\n`packages/storage-browser/tests/phase-6a-creator-successor-product.pw.ts`, and\nthe cold activation/reopen cases in\n`tests/phase-6a-creator-successor-activation-red.test.ts`, become exact 0b0 RED\nwhen no independently authenticated pin is supplied: they fail before room\nauthority or activation with `D110C_FLOOR_MIGRATION_REQUIRED` or the named\navailability owner. Their original success remains retained only in the paired\ncase that supplies a separately authenticated application/account test pin.\nThis changes no D.108 evidence retrospectively; it freezes how those same\ngolden-path controls are interpreted after the new mandatory freshness owner\nexists.\n\nFocused gates cover a deterministic in-memory hostile room store and a separate\nmodel provider, real browser room reopen with an injected account-authority\ntest implementation, creator trust/close/adoption retained vectors, exact\npublic source shape, package builds/typechecks, exact-owner lint/format/diff,\nprotected paths/stashes, and signed/pushed evidence. T