the public contract. Deterministic RED then replaces prose inference:\n92853\tone genuine first-transition fixture must prove that the current public API has\n92854\tno durable-complete/no-head-swap capability and no non-activating pending cold\n92855\trecovery owner, failing with exact token\n92856\t`D110C_0B0A_STAGED_HANDOFF_SEAM_MISSING`. RED must not alter product source or\n92857\trun a retained campaign.\n92858\t\n92859\tGREEN acceptance is exact and Node-only:\n92860\t\n92861\t- after genuine stage, the candidate is complete and fully authenticated, the\n92862\t  AHE head remains the prior exact head, no provider call has occurred, and no\n92863\t  successor owner has activated;\n92864\t- publish refuses a missing, foreign, replayed, duplicated, already-consumed,\n92865\t  cross-handle, wrong-head, or mutated staged capability and preserves exact\n92866\t  existing failure custody;\n92867\t- publish performs one exact head CAS and resolves an ambiguous result by\n92868\t  authenticated equality, never by assuming success;\n92869\t- cold pending recovery covers both provider/AHE orderings, candidate absent,\n92870\t  candidate incomplete, wrong previous/next provider anchor tuple, equivalent\n92871\t  duplicate Complete candidates, different-closure true fork, malformed\n92872\t  stores, abandoned pre-pending candidate, and ambiguous CAS, without\n92873\t  activation and without deriving either expected tuple from room storage;\n92874\t- a tests-only deterministic decision model composes stage, a modeled pending\n92875\t  boundary, publish, a modeled stable boundary, and recovery to prove that the\n92876\t  Node calls support the frozen six-step order. It does not add the provider\n92877\t  public contract, rewrite the product, or claim the complete 0b0 crash matrix;\n92878\t- the old one-call API, exact module export roster, and retained product-owner\n92879\t  source predicates keep their previously proved semantics; adding the two new\n92880\t  non-root subpaths updates only the exact package-export-map snapshots that\n92881\t  enumerate every `@ts-drp/node` export;\n92882\t- no provider object crosses into Node or protocol-v3, and no wire record,\n92883\t  schema, digest, authority, dependency, threshold, rollback generation,\n92884\t  availability rule, or public product capability beyond the reviewed Node\n92885\t  lifecycle seam changes; and\n92886\t- exact-owner source-shape tests, Node builds/typechecks, focused genuine\n92887\t  runtime tests, all retained creator adoption/activation/reopen and cleanup\n92888\t  tests, lint/format/diff, protected paths, stashes, signed commits, pushed refs,\n92889\t  and self-excluding evidence manifests pass. Product/example browser controls\n92890\t  remain unchanged and are rerun by 0b0 after its product rewrite.\n92891\t\n92892\tAfter signed/pushed GREEN, one formal Grok/Kimi/Opus review covers plan → RED →\n92893\tGREEN causality, the additive compatibility boundary, capability custody,\n92894\tnon-activating recovery, and retained behavior. Only then may 0b0 resume and\n92895\timplement provider initialization, product orchestration, expected-head\n92896\tactivation/reopen gates, classification, the full crash matrix, the authorized\n92897\tsource-governance updates, and the already frozen focused/retained gates.\n92898\tD.110c-0b0a does not implement the freshness provider, rewrite the product,\n92899\tchange existing creator-adoption-commit contracts, add the bounded checkpoint\n92900\topener, perform repeated rollover or pruning, evolve the archive, or run any\n92901\tlong campaign.\n92902\t\n92903\tThe first D.110c-0b0a plan review inspected signed/pushed commit\n92904\t`7f6d05d366466a7e1c5e0a6e37d5bb1f8cab1e29` in a clean detached checkout.\n92905\tPrompt SHA-256 is\n92906\t`64a777daf5218d89cc28e13aba6886bac1adb52a831337de1969042170665eb5`.\n92907\tGrok 4.6/high completed with `stop_reason=end_turn` after active inspection but\n92908\tplaced explanatory prose before its terminal JSON, so the runner honestly\n92909\tclassified it `NO_VERDICT`; its public terminal content was `BLOCKED` with two\n92910\tP1 and one P2. Grok event/public/status SHA-256 values are\n92911\t`3907660e807de0d48f77d6914546df71d4e5cf40f84f01ae91455e8ffcd4575f`,\n92912\t`d2b071cb505bf9d3937a9591af32c1b472536de3db01d8894f6e99aca99d5d8e`, and\n92913\t`1b712e1a8bdcc02a943e6d5589b92503e960fb5acdd6c48eac6730f1f8fa9102`.\n92914\tDirect Kimi K3 with the exact 100-step control, session\n92915\t`session_9e4333d2-a1bb-496c-b489-0b92b51b3dc7`, returned `PASS`, P0=0/P1=0/P2=2;\n92916\tits exported-session SHA-256 is\n92917\t`63a76d4f0c54a985e138e5f9fcd4831b40c808dd985890bc4444a09e58abc90a`.\n92918\tOpus xhigh session `2cfa1f8e-7271-4643-b892-b434a54ca752` returned `BLOCKED`,\n92919\tP0=0/P1=3/P2=2; terminal SHA-256 is\n92920\t`3e7a818b46b9c65de2c967bc92c0a498f47b63eebcfaae70fe9f6ae941d3c231`.\n92921\t\n92922\tThe blocking union is accepted and corrected in one batch. D.110c-0b0a is\n92923\tNode-only and uses new subpaths so the existing commit export and retained\n92924\tproduct-source contracts remain unchanged. It freezes exact operation and\n92925\tinput/result names, treats same-tuple/same-closure retry leftovers as equivalent\n92926\twith deterministic generation selection, treats different-closure matches as a\n92927\ttrue fork, and explicitly leaves product/provider orchestration and hot/cold\n92928\texpected-head activation gates to 0b0. The P2 union is dispositioned in the\n92929\tsame correction: provider tuples are distinguished from AHE locators; the\n92930\tcompatibility wrapper is documented as non-freshness; and 0b0 owns the\n92931\tsource-governance rewrite. Because these corrections change executable scope\n92932\tand the public Node boundary, the single permitted Grok/Kimi/Opus confirmation\n92933\tmust inspect the signed correction. No later prose-only round is permitted.\n92934\t\n92935\tThe single confirmation inspected signed/pushed correction\n92936\t`4f893654e6456ca94384277054ac51fb2df4413d` from a clean detached checkout.\n92937\tPrompt SHA-256 is\n92938\t`8ee96fd63c82be173f4b887f5937d0e19b5268d0791e472f84d6d0f9cbfcf96a`.\n92939\tGrok 4.6/high completed with `stop_reason=end_turn` and emitted an explicit\n92940\t`PASS`, P0=0/P1=0/P2=2 JSON after inspection prose; because the prose preceded\n92941\tthe terminal object, the strict runner honestly classified the invocation\n92942\t`NO_VERDICT`. It did not cancel, time out, or report a blocking finding. Grok\n92943\tevent/public/status SHA-256 values are\n92944\t`d5417ff1c8d47d8a9a69f47c7d70043411f4647c4a241e2a0496bfe17d39d5f0`,\n92945\t`c74436f74b5994ef8e00456d840c938005613ea5fe5aea3d29bf7bf1f9e9b259`, and\n92946\t`b7edf022d694a0205ec7295679baf171e9f32666747c79036a0f40a5bd304fec`.\n92947\tDirect Kimi K3 session `session_8c87a776-6622-428e-a2f9-ad6f15c34263`\n92948\twith the exact 100-step control returned `PASS`, P0=0/P1=0/P2=2; its exported\n92949\tsession SHA-256 is\n92950\t`f4330108c8b1c51afce19c1443634ab2f8f50376f3100e92700a9d1947089e73`.\n92951\tOpus xhigh session `04a793cc-81de-4586-8047-f8dc9e346b1a` returned `PASS`,\n92952\tP0=0/P1=0/P2=3; its recorded terminal SHA-256 is\n92953\t`a40143d3800a977e01aaf2fa0b7f0b5fda5218d15bc9df97c3adedf7f6b7625d`.\n92954\t\n92955\tThe blocking confirmation union is empty. The P2 union is dispositioned\n92956\tmechanically without another review: the RED freeze states publish's literal\n92957\tlifecycle/recovery values and exact encoded generation-ID ordering; an\n92958\talready-new AHE is compared by authenticated successor trust rather than\n92959\tgeneration locator; the full package-export-map snapshot is updated for the\n92960\ttwo additive subpaths; equivalent unselected-candidate reclamation is owned by\n92961\t0b0/0b1 census work; and the retained one-call API wording no longer implies\n92962\tthat it wraps the new operations. The approximate count of later product-owner\n92963\tcontracts remains bookkeeping for 0b0, which must enumerate the actual changed\n92964\tpredicates when it rewrites the product. No finding changes executable scope,\n92965\tauthority, workload, or a hard acceptance gate. The D.110c-0b0a plan gate is\n92966\taccepted; deterministic RED is next.\n92967\t\n92968\tThe deterministic D.110c-0b0a RED then ran exactly once from accepted plan HEAD\n92969\t`c47927f515f1182b6bc6a711e85fb696d3effe1b`. The sole selected test and file,\n92970\t`tests/phase-6b-d110c-0b0a-staged-handoff-red.test.ts`, opened a genuine\n92971\tfirst-transition fixture, authenticated its successor intent, observed the\n92972\tretained one-call commit perform exactly one old-to-new AHE head swap, and\n92973\tproved that neither reviewed stage nor recovery subpath exists. It then failed\n92974\tonly with exact token `D110C_0B0A_STAGED_HANDOFF_SEAM_MISSING`: one selected,\n92975\tzero passed, one failed, zero pending, zero unexpected errors, and no campaign\n92976\ttitle. The JSON report is authoritative and has `success:false`; Vitest's JSON\n92977\toutput-file invocation anomalously returned shell status 0, which is recorded\n92978\tseparately and does not convert the failed report into a pass. Source and\n92979\treport SHA-256 values are\n92980\t`295515e5fc3dc980c0b40291632ff5c39e7d608acb73fec59cb7fa2152820ce9` and\n92981\t`db4dcd8218055f0d1ab323634faa74511bc977ac244de3c9a4265388db4d9ac9`.\n92982\tThe causal matrix matches the frozen RED exactly; no production file changed,\n92983\tno retained or long test ran, and GREEN may now implement only the accepted\n92984\tNode seam.\n92985\t\n92986\tThis exact owner-selection design is signed and pushed before one bounded Grok\n92987\t4.6/high, standard direct Kimi K3 with\n92988\t`KIMI_LOOP_MAX_STEPS_PER_TURN=100`, and Opus xhigh review. Only P0/P1 blocks;\n92989\tmaterial findings are corrected in one batch with at most one confirmation if\n92990\tscope, causal acceptance, or the public authority contract changes. No\n92991\tproduction edit, RED, Fable, collaboration subagent, or long workload runs\n92992\tbefore that gate is accepted.\n92993\t\n92994\tThe owner-selection review inspected signed/pushed plan-only commit\n92995\t`65912fbc6fc128fb4cc648c7f028924bd36cb865` from\n92996\t`.logs/d110c-0b0-owner-design-review-65912fbc`; prompt SHA-256 is\n92997\t`e56c1c4e9dcb8bf80d5dd050d967b22bc8601a4a67aebfb23b24d0fc5f413384`.\n92998\tGrok 4.6/high completed normally with P0=0/P1=0/P2=4; its event and public\n92999\tresult SHA-256 values are\n93000\t`b959c4375e71bb144bb09499c0aeb9481d27568faf7e0ddad9a3ed675e93fe00`\n93001\tand `47de316cf28a041a6111c2a23532f1f91750af90314f5cbc1fb58898af058fdb`.\n93002\tStandard direct Kimi K3 session\n93003\t`session_a38e5a00-207c-41c2-9300-a075f4cc7105`, with the exact 100-step\n93004\tcontrol, returned P0=0/P1=0/P2=2; its exported session SHA-256 is\n93005\t`7691f29dc5b6e7baca8b4cf870b364d93097ce441b52b794f1b25bf1098e0c04`.\n93006\tOpus xhigh session `713c2922-9d41-43fd-a804-7da32e937450` returned\n93007\tP0=0/P1=1/P2=3; its transcript SHA-256 is\n93008\t`cee5595e82c6627218b17246598514aa1a89466ff4c0584b8315924b97f9e7f9`.\n93009\t\n93010\tThe blocking finding is accepted. Local genesis bytes cannot prove that a\n93011\tprovider-less room was never advanced, so ordinary reopen may never create a\n93012\tfloor—even when local storage presents authentic epoch 0. The correction\n93013\trequires an account-side create-if-never-seen act for new rooms, makes all\n93014\tprovider-less reopen migration-required, forbids scope reuse, and requires an\n93015\tindependent pin for explicit legacy migration. The P2 union is dispositioned in\n93016\tthe same batch: step-4 equality authorizes step-5 retirement while step 6 gates\n93017\tpublication; the redundant transition commitment is removed; pending recovery\n93018\tdominates mismatch classification; same-next reopen follows the winning pending\n93019\trather than retrying begin-CAS; 0b0 uses the existing first-transition opener\n93020\tand leaves the dual-record protocol opener to 0b1; creator-publisher versus\n93021\tparticipant floor ownership is explicit; and erasing room deletion remains\n93022\tunsupported without a later tombstone policy. Because these changes alter the\n93023\tsecurity initialization predicate and public capability operations, one\n93024\tbounded confirmation of the signed correction is required. No closure prose\n93025\treceives another review.\n93026\t\n93027\tThe single confirmation inspected signed/pushed commit\n93028\t`49e8dcff1751662d8039ec138c56e72e3af1050a` from\n93029\t`.logs/d110c-0b0-owner-confirmation-49e8dcff`; prompt SHA-256 is\n93030\t`03ce567b0834905bdeb44b6ba605114160861322a126541402eec3e90be3f6f2`.\n93031\tGrok 4.6/high completed normally with P0=0/P1=0/P2=0; its event and public\n93032\tresult SHA-256 values are\n93033\t`918190bcb4671a8f933d95828a748a804b1145b7c21d3ba76e784f8c5001c95f`\n93034\tand `c0f6a0f395c2c2996498c4b15c4d45a4a94582bf5b65968fd3784824fd465fc1`.\n93035\tStandard direct Kimi K3 session\n93036\t`session_3fe115c9-2baf-404b-98cc-a7a2395c0ea0`, with the exact 100-step\n93037\tcontrol, returned P0=0/P1=0/P2=0; its exported session SHA-256 is\n93038\t`732ad623cf8049d617a1585b937ba63adde5eb47a350ab1ea6b96d5ce40ff061`.\n93039\tOpus xhigh session `62965e4c-1c33-4cbf-b9a2-e00b615d7303` returned\n93040\tP0=0/P1=0/P2=2; its transcript SHA-256 is\n93041\t`bbf8c00da8113a5ece09af118093ee0c03a62eedf95cdd3011065cdf30fc7e7e`.\n93042\tThe two nonblocking wording findings are dispositioned without another round:\n93043\tcreate/migrate CAS refusal is explicitly `D110C_FLOOR_CONFLICT`, and no method\n93044\tmay accept an absent floor in ordinary reopen regardless of local epoch. The\n93045\tblocking confirmation union is empty, the exact design is accepted, and the\n93046\tnext state is `D110C_0A_PLAN_READY`.\n93047\t\n93048\tThe four prerequisite decisions, including the newly demonstrated 0b0\n93049\tfreshness-floor authority question, are reviewed before their production edits;\n93050\teach executable sub-slice receives its own bounded causal RED and GREEN. The\n93051\tumbrella's minimum functional GREEN is not satisfied until\n93052\tD.110c-0a/0b0/0b/0b1/0c/a/b/c jointly prove one genuine room completes epoch 0→1,\n93053\trestart/reopen, epoch 1→2,\n93054\tcontinued issue/publish after epoch 2, and cold recovery with exact application\n93055\tstate, ACL, writer authority, current anchor/trust, compact history,\n93056\tarchive-index root, snapshots, journals, and operation accounting. A second\n93057\tclose that only returns an epoch number is not acceptance.\n93058\t\n93059\t##### Retained long-horizon and golden-path acceptance\n93060\t\n93061\tD.110c-d must prove, in a fresh process where required, all of the following:\n93062\t\n93063\t- at least 100 genuine transitions on one production room, with strictly\n93064\t  increasing epochs and authenticated anchor/QC/cut lineage;\n93065\t- exact compact-history root and size extension at every step, with no skipped,\n93066\t  duplicated, reordered, or substituted epoch and no same-anchor double close;\n93067\t- real issue/admit/apply/publish work before and after selected transitions,\n93068\t  exact aggregate operation accounting, exact application state, and an\n93069\t  independently derived semantic digest;\n93070\t- restart/reopen at selected pre-close, post-close, pre-adoption,\n93071\t  post-adoption, and post-prune boundaries, including offline/rebase outbox and\n93072\t  first-successful-publication continuity;\n93073\t- pruning only after verified adoption, two complete rollback generations,\n93074\t  satisfied availability, complete outbox classification, and authenticated\n93075\t  archive/snapshot dependencies; refusal and crash may retain too much but may\n93076\t  not delete too much;\n93077\t- bounded active-owner, registration, close-handle, displaced-predecessor,\n93078\t  hot/control closure, snapshot/quarantine, issuance/outbox, AHE\n93079\t  generation/blob, rollback, and runtime structure census, without moving\n93080\t  unbounded control data into a journal or sibling owner. Intentionally archival\n93081\t  application/history bytes receive a separate exact segment/byte census and\n93082\t  are never counted as bounded hot state;\n93083\t- a fresh-process, during-execution, post-GC memory series over repeated\n93084\t  same-room rollovers, paired with exact work and digest assertions. Its exact\n93085\t  sample window, workload, watchdog, epsilon, and absolute ceiling require a\n93086\t  separately reviewed freeze before execution; D.110a's distinct-room values\n93087\t  are preserved as evidence but are not silently reused as this contract; and\n93088\t- two real semantic controls using the same production lifecycle: an\n93089\t  MMORPG-style world whose current state and authority continue across\n93090\t  rotations, and a Discord-shaped room whose messages span genuine epochs and\n93091\t  whose current work continues after safe pruning. D.110c must produce the\n93092\t  latter without synthetic archive rows; actual evolving archive roots and\n93093\t  cold paging remain a separately reviewed Phase-7 control because the current\n93094\t  creator-close wire requires the archive root to remain unchanged.\n93095\t\n93096\tPhase 7a's one-million-message cold-join gate is downstream acceptance, not a\n93097\tD.110c shortcut. Before implementation it must explicitly reslice the current\n93098\tarchive-root equality contract if genuine segment production requires the root\n93099\tto advance. It then ingests the genuinely multi-epoch Discord control after\n93100\tearly epochs have been safely pruned, authenticates its archive lineage, and\n93101\tproves O(hot + window) network bytes. One oversized epoch, prebuilt archive\n93102\tsegments, or fixture-authored epoch records is invalid. Neither the Discord\n93103\tgolden path nor age-independent cold join is claimed until that downstream gate\n93104\tis green.\n93105\t\n93106\t##### Retained gates, evidence, review, and debt disposition\n93107\t\n93108\tEvery sub-slice retains the complete affected protocol-v3 seal vectors,\n93109\tPhase-5e creator seal/close, Phase-6a adoption/commit/activation/reopen,\n93110\tD.108d2/e v3-room governance, D.109a-f cleanup/reclamation,\n93111\tsnapshot-quarantine, live-journal parity, issuance, storage Node/browser, and\n93112\tD.110a non-consuming validator suites; affected package builds and source\n93113\ttypechecks; exact-owner lint/format/diff/source-shape checks; and protected-path,\n93114\t26-stash, process/port, signed-commit, pushed-ref, changed-path, hash, and\n93115\tself-excluding manifest custody. D.110a's full worker and preflight are\n93116\tpermanently excluded: both identities are consumed and neither may run again.\n93117\t\n93118\tThe current audit/plan checkpoint is signed and pushed before one bounded\n93119\tGrok 4.6/high, standard direct Kimi K3 with\n93120\t`KIMI_LOOP_MAX_STEPS_PER_TURN=100`, and Opus xhigh review. If Grok cancels,\n93121\tresume that exact session. Only P0/P1 findings block; P2 receives an owner and\n93122\tdisposition without recursive prose review. No additional Fable or any\n93123\tcollaboration subagent runs. Because this is a high-risk production lifecycle, each later\n93124\tproduction GREEN receives the governing final plan→RED→GREEN review, and the\n93125\tlong-horizon workload receives a reviewed immutable freeze before its sole\n93126\tconsuming execution.\n93127\t\n93128\tThe umbrella-plan review of signed commit\n93129\t`d7c102b8e3cb7beb921fb67bc86e8ab096424b28` is preserved honestly at\n93130\t`.logs/d110c-plan-review-d7c102b8`. Kimi session\n93131\t`e4a22064-e892-41af-9044-e403e8c1a0bf` returned an immediate authentication\n93132\t401 and therefore `NO_VERDICT`. Grok's initial service run cancelled; the exact\n93133\tsession `01a05fcf-470f-7222-9d6f-176a228a15a0` was resumed and returned zero\n93134\tP0/P1 plus three P2 findings. Opus session\n93135\t`6496e64d-1bb3-4ff8-ade2-16ab1d4a449f` returned one P1: browser\n93136\t`sealEvidence`, `voteSlots`, `signerState`, and `voteOutbox` had no deletion\n93137\towner and were absent from the bounded census. The corrections above close that\n93138\tP1 and disposition Grok's P2 findings by qualifying the 6c-r compatibility\n93139\tclaim, naming browser seal adapters/migration, assigning snapshot substitution\n93140\tto D.110c-a, and adding hot close/verify/commit consumers to D.110c-0b. No prior\n93141\tverdict is relabelled as having reviewed this later amendment.\n93142\t\n93143\tThe first formal comparative-design review inspected signed/pushed commit\n93144\t`871c7782fcfcc0abbc8acaed81bef92fa7c00b50` from evidence root\n93145\t`.logs/d110c-0b-hiero-plan-review-871c7782`; prompt SHA-256 is\n93146\t`c4b684e40fac1fefee9f8ca89fb5f67c0223c2f586642d6f05c653e5e9086f14`.\n93147\tGrok 4.6/high session `01a05feb-255e-77e3-bd6a-b15f673e3e71` completed\n93148\tnormally with P0=0/P1=1/P2=2: the blocking finding correctly identified that\n93149\tthe original 0b1 RED demanded three genuine transitions before 0a/a/b could\n93150\tproduce them. Opus xhigh session `cdf1629a-cfc3-4479-9539-c8dca17fbcf2`\n93151\treturned P0=0/P1=0/P2=3 and independently identified the same ordering\n93152\tambiguity, the exported exactly-one inspector boundary, and the difference\n93153\tbetween the room expected-head tuple and AHE storage head. Direct Kimi K3\n93154\tsession `6b472f97-58bf-4957-b4ac-3e527067a374`, invoked with both 100-step\n93155\tcontrols, failed immediately with provider 401\n93156\t`invalid_authentication_error` and is honestly `NO_VERDICT`; it did not inspect\n93157\tthe plan. The correction above sequences executable 0b1 after 0a/a/b GREEN,\n93158\tpreserves the exported exactly-one predicates behind a first stop-check, and\n93159\trequires a caller-authenticated room head distinct from hostile storage/AHE\n93160\thead. Because the ordering correction changes