, P0=0/P1=0/P2=2, and `D110C_0A_PLAN_READY`. Prompt, streamed-event,\n93190\tand stderr SHA-256 values are\n93191\t`1f36bd420644a79e2123cd5096ec5805925323cc0defa8a79bbaf75bca6deeea`,\n93192\t`099f246393a3f7054769107eb4839a00911fc4379d6c5e2a46b15c9153399725`,\n93193\tand `ab3f2cf2b73f1d60a7b9af1229fe2aaca3b36f91fe68a0310e5b992fc8338106`.\n93194\tIts P2 dispositions are nonblocking: prior reviewer-session hashes were outside\n93195\tits deliberate no-peer-output inspection scope and remain plan-custodian\n93196\tmetadata; the authenticated freshness-carrier stop-check already precedes any\n93197\t0b1 RED assertion that depends on such a carrier. The D.110c comparative-design\n93198\tgate was therefore accepted at that checkpoint. It authorized D.110c-0a\n93199\tplanning/RED next at that time, not 0b1 implementation, production behavior\n93200\toutside 0a, or any campaign. The later expressly authorized Fable source audit\n93201\tbelow does not relabel Kimi as having reviewed its new evidence and\n93202\tprospectively pauses production RED until 0b0's exact design is reviewed.\n93203\t\n93204\tThe one expressly authorized Fable 5.1/high read-only advisory run used session\n93205\t`eefd0856-c660-4cc6-aa98-3c41eb863316`, spawned no subagents, and returned\n93206\t`CHANGES_REQUIRED`. Its prompt and raw-result SHA-256 values are\n93207\t`7f21200678b0accc3ad6e77b1bc986202bf8be2f2c2eef33bb1e718e4545cd65`\n93208\tand `b42f7e453175119315437c6b614ea6f4f70f299c6484ba26682b13e7dc386935`.\n93209\tThe corrected audit adopts its demonstrated epoch-0 seal, stale active owner,\n93210\tmissing pending-resume/product owner, and cold-chain findings. It rejects only\n93211\tthe suggested acceptance of exact linear active-closure growth: the user's\n93212\tbounded durable-structure requirement instead creates D.110c-0b. This one-off\n93213\trun is complete and does not authorize another Fable invocation.\n93214\t\n93215\tThe separately and expressly authorized one-off Fable 5.1/high comparative\n93216\tresearch used CLI session `eb63f14c-826b-48f3-80b7-5fa40818620e`, spawned no\n93217\tsubagents, changed no files, and returned `CHANGES_REQUIRED`/\n93218\t`D110C_0B_DESIGN_READY: NO`. Its prompt and raw-result SHA-256 values are\n93219\t`96159e1917d73b3529c5fc51633de1cfe1d9b5410be69c0c65f5b14c001277c5`\n93220\tand `11340aefc10f4d9e7302de4dbc23c98984c9734a32381525ca80aa4052abb0e6`;\n93221\tstderr was empty. The audit adopts its confirmed epoch-0 opener, linear closure,\n93222\tfour unowned seal-store families, fixed creator-authority simplification,\n93223\tfreshness caveat, certified-profile stop boundary, and proposal-versus-code\n93224\tthreshold/wire cautions. Its “not ready” disposition is closed at plan level by\n93225\tnaming the bounded dual-anchor v1 design, exact authenticated expected-head\n93226\trequirement, active-versus-rollback retention boundary, D.110c-0b1 stop gate,\n93227\tand seal-store owner/census above. It is advisory evidence, not a substitute for\n93228\tthe governing Grok/Kimi/Opus review, and does not authorize another Fable run.\n93229\t\n93230\tThe later, separately and expressly authorized one-off Fable 5.1/high parallel\n93231\tresearch inspected head `c11823b34ae214fe8347cfee1f3d910c2a10a97f` in CLI\n93232\tsession `bc78b8b6-7bc8-49bb-92a0-85a671911522`. It completed normally after 51\n93233\tturns with `claude-fable-5-1`, high effort, zero spawned subagents, zero\n93234\tpermission denials, and no repository changes. Prompt, full report, and session\n93235\ttranscript SHA-256 values are\n93236\t`f78b89685909bfd12847383b53da5446375d7fb87bcc3114d0bd65fe9c95813a`,\n93237\t`0eb60c3f8509becc97b26718cbcfe89384c4d2197fd3717d05733412bb4096f3`,\n93238\tand `76e66c610cae6045e7ed560bc367aba30b09e1886301b395c8185a04000235ab`.\n93239\tIt independently confirmed that all three inspected upstream main heads still\n93240\tequal the audit pins. Its material dispositions are prospective and do not\n93241\treopen immutable evidence:\n93242\t\n93243\t- P1 freshness is **accepted**: the deferred carrier stop-check now has a\n93244\t  deterministic negative answer, so D.110c-0b0 owns the new authority decision\n93245\t  before production RED;\n93246\t- P1 predecessor-QC authority is **closed by clarification**, not a new naked\n93247\t  authority constructor: the already-bounded newest rollback closure retains\n93248\t  and reopens the genuine epoch-N-1 trust used by epoch-relative 0a QC\n93249\t  verification;\n93250\t- P1 equivocation is **accepted as a predicate correction**: a lone valid fork\n93251\t  is detectable only against the authenticated floor, while two present records\n93252\t  remain an ambiguity failure;\n93253\t- the threshold, compressed-proof, reconnect-floor, new-opener, ≤53-peak\n93254\t  accumulator, and AHE census P2s are incorporated above or were already owned;\n93255\t  and\n93256\t- a separate local source audit found the public browser evidence-serving\n93257\t  selector lacks epoch, so the 0a plan must review that compatibility boundary\n93258\t  explicitly.\n93259\t\n93260\tThis advisory result is not a substitute for the governing Grok/Kimi/Opus\n93261\thigh-risk review. The amendment checkpoint is the 0b0 **plan** review only; it\n93262\tdoes not select the floor owner or unlock 0a production. No production edit\n93263\tbegins until the subsequent 0b0 owner-selection design and the bounded 0a plan\n93264\thave the required accepted review. This explicit authorization is consumed;\n93265\tno additional Fable run is authorized.\n93266\t\n93267\tThe governing amendment review inspected signed/pushed plan-only commit\n93268\t`610d0f9ea73b672a3bcbb565f0b85da86488e693` from\n93269\t`.logs/d110c-0b0-amendment-review-610d0f9e`; prompt SHA-256 is\n93270\t`eb2d184fb16a4eac2fdeb2f4a9562b244b56d6d3645a5e63578cee45f6039264`.\n93271\tGrok 4.6/high completed normally without cancellation and returned\n93272\tP0=0/P1=0/P2=2. Session events and public-result SHA-256 values are\n93273\t`309799714fe890014ab50407fc85aa25d6214ecd70f9719f7e081e2f81ee7223`\n93274\tand `a32327e206e95463bacf358ef42bd949915fa657e99f94517047e935fdc817c6`.\n93275\tStandard direct Kimi K3 session\n93276\t`session_7614f048-b3be-47c8-a8a3-e9d1d47dabb3`, with\n93277\t`KIMI_LOOP_MAX_STEPS_PER_TURN=100`, returned P0=0/P1=0/P2=1; its exported\n93278\tsession SHA-256 is\n93279\t`8137630944b813488e131e1753e340bff38f93b11b05d204f45100d590bbd37d`.\n93280\tOpus xhigh session `6c6dc13f-7534-42f5-8210-e8e93a91d73c` returned\n93281\tP0=0/P1=1/P2=3; its transcript SHA-256 is\n93282\t`c2f9f5cf86d38b0ed781a44612e53480bbde401b0e7c541d9e01d55290b087aa`.\n93283\t\n93284\tThe single blocking finding is accepted: the floor law was one-directional,\n93285\tso a floor that stopped advancing could authorize the matching stale\n93286\tgeneration. The correction above makes authenticated room-head installation\n93287\tand floor advancement atomic in both directions, refuses a lagging floor, and\n93288\trequires generalized close/adoption owners to preserve that law. The P2 union\n93289\tis also dispositioned without a separate prose round: latest-floor equality is\n93290\tonly for the proposed current head; predecessor authentication terminates at\n93291\tthe immediate retained rollback record without recursively verifying its own\n93292\tQC; the accumulator ceiling is corrected from 54 to 53 peaks; the floor owner\n93293\tgets O(1) growth, retirement, and D.110c-c/d census obligations; and this is\n93294\tnamed the 0b0 plan review rather than the later owner-selection design review.\n93295\tBecause the accepted P1 changes a hard security acceptance predicate, one\n93296\tbounded confirmation of this signed correction is required. It is the only\n93297\tconfirmation; no bookkeeping or closure prose receives another review.\n93298\t\n93299\tThat single confirmation inspected signed/pushed commit\n93300\t`340a66466768133aee20493186d46bf2c8e76512` from\n93301\t`.logs/d110c-0b0-confirmation-340a6646`; prompt SHA-256 is\n93302\t`69a23e6d5ec4e3e25938d833cc87b1d862af5d55234bbda6a5d10aef338d6336`.\n93303\tGrok 4.6/high completed normally with P0=0/P1=0/P2=0; its events and public\n93304\tresult SHA-256 values are\n93305\t`2711e1c52eee96be707294fc518e0f7a01bf923ba4688f4d221800a91fa1fe08`\n93306\tand `bf054af72a2736c146719b19a577d3a6b93e1bc8310fea30148918af6d299041`.\n93307\tStandard direct Kimi K3 session\n93308\t`session_4452eabe-19de-490d-ae69-892da0b6f4f2`, with the exact 100-step\n93309\tcontrol, returned P0=0/P1=0/P2=0; its exported session SHA-256 is\n93310\t`c37902733b1e21619785a9da734193cffa8f314cbae3c61c93785861c894d847`.\n93311\tOpus xhigh session `679bfe17-46ba-400b-82eb-6aba41076a4d` returned\n93312\tP0=0/P1=0/P2=1; its transcript SHA-256 is\n93313\t`893d7a1f5d2690018b99269f1713b3852a566dfee5b24495eb51dd1fd0dca378`.\n93314\tIts attempted shell-monitor call was denied as required by the read-only tool\n93315\tpolicy; it completed the review from the captured exact commit diff and local\n93316\tread-only sources. The sole P2 is assigned to the next 0b0 owner-selection\n93317\tdesign: crash completion of a pending floor advance may not derive the floor\n93318\tvalue from the hostile local head/checkpoint. It does not change this plan\n93319\tcheckpoint or trigger another confirmation. The blocking confirmation union is\n93320\tempty and the exact next state is `D110C_0B0_OWNER_SELECTION_READY`.\n93321\t\n93322\tDebt disposition is explicit: D.110c owns repeated same-room rollover,\n93323\tepoch-relative creator seal custody, bounded authenticated current-trust\n93324\trecovery/control closure, durable pending-adoption resume, and the product room\n93325\tloop. None can be deferred to Phase 6d or hidden in Phase 7. Phase 6d still owns\n93326\tlegacy-finality retention. Phase 7 owns the separately reviewed archive-root\n93327\tevolution/segmentation, availability receipts, cold paging, and deletion UX;\n93328\tits long-lived-room acceptance is blocked on D.110c's genuine producer. D.109f\n93329\tremains the synthetic durable-maintenance proof and D.110a remains the\n93330\tdistinct-room churn/per-handoff memory proof. Until all D.110c acceptance is\n93331\tgreen, the repository may claim epoch awareness and one genuine handoff, but\n93332\tnot a repeatable-epoch lifecycle or Phase-6 closure. Until Phase 7 consumes that\n93333\tproducer, it may not claim the complete long-lived Discord/archive golden path.\n93334\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b68b30f-133f-4078-a9a7-ee7aeeec8953","uuid":"c242b697-94ec-49be-aa77-5bf641c67487","timestamp":"2026-09-02T08:25:26.278Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/aristotle/Documents/Projects/ts-drp-1/docs/production-hardening/production-hardening-tdd-plan-v2.md","content":"##### D.110c-0b0a staged adoption and pending-recovery prerequisite\n\nThe first 0b0 GREEN composition audit found a narrower prerequisite that the\naccepted owner design did not make executable. At RED evidence HEAD\n`685611728ecfe37bbdb09369f245f9a909fcf776`, the exported\n`commitCreatorSuccessorAdoption()` consumes its one-use authenticated intent,\nstages/completes the candidate generation, and swaps the AHE head in the same\ncall. It cannot expose the required durable-complete-but-not-published state in\nwhich the application installs the provider pending record. Conversely,\n`reopenCreatorSuccessorAdoption()` authenticates only the already-adopted\nthree-generation epoch-1 shape and activates it in the same call. It cannot\nauthenticate or finish a provider-selected pending candidate without live\nactivation. Therefore expected-head plumbing alone cannot implement the frozen\nsix-step protocol or its old-head/new-head crash rows. Reordering the existing\ncalls is not a repair: committing the AHE first creates an unrecoverable\nfloor-behind/head-ahead window, while installing pending first can leave no\ndurably complete selected candidate after a crash.\n\nThis is a demonstrated production composition/API seam, not permission to\nweaken crash acceptance or hide provider I/O in Node. **D.110c-0b0a** owns it,\nblocks resumption of 0b0 GREEN, and is due before any focused 0b0 GREEN run,\nD.110c-a production work, or multi-epoch execution. Its source owner is the\ncreator adoption lifecycle across\n`packages/node/src/creator-adoption-commit.ts`,\n`packages/node/src/creator-adoption.ts`,\n`packages/node/src/creator-adoption-activate.ts`, two new non-root Node subpaths\n`creator-adoption-stage` and `creator-adoption-recover`, and their private\nopaque-capability registries under `packages/node/src/internal/`. The existing\n`creator-adoption-commit` export roster and the product orchestrator in\n`examples/v3-room/src/index.ts` are retained unchanged by 0b0a. Existing\nexploratory uncommitted 0b0 edits are non-evidence and receive no acceptance; no\nadditional production edit or focused GREEN execution may occur until this\nprerequisite's plan gate is accepted.\n\nThe selected compatibility direction is additive and phase-separated:\n\n1. New non-root subpath `@ts-drp/node/creator-adoption-stage` exports exactly\n   `stageCreatorSuccessorAdoption` and\n   `publishStagedCreatorSuccessorAdoption`. Stage consumes exact input\n   `{handle,intent}`, writes and authenticates the complete next generation,\n   leaves the exact old AHE head unchanged, and returns exact success keys\n   `{capability,descriptor,lifecycle,ok,recovery}` with\n   `lifecycle:\"successor-staged\"` and `recovery:\"pending-old\"`. The capability\n   is a distinct owner-bound, one-use opaque type; it is not accepted by the\n   existing commit or activation owners. Publish consumes exact input\n   `{capability,handle}`, performs the exact old-head-to-next-head CAS, resolves\n   ambiguous storage results only through authenticated reopen/equality, and\n   returns the existing prepared-activation success shape\n   `{capability,descriptor,head,lifecycle,ok,recovery}` with\n   `lifecycle:\"successor-prepared\"` and `recovery:\"active-new\"`. Both operations use\n   exact failure keys `{detail,kind,ok}` and perform no provider I/O or live\n   activation.\n2. New non-root subpath `@ts-drp/node/creator-adoption-recover` exports exactly\n   `recoverPendingCreatorSuccessorAdoption`. Its exact input keys are\n   `{authenticationProfile,catalog,detachedSignature,exactCanonicalAnchorPreimageBytes,exactCanonicalParametersCarrierBytes,expectedNextRoomHead,expectedPreviousRoomHead,pinnedGenesisAnchorDigest,snapshotDeclaration,snapshotStore,store}`.\n   The two expected values are copied exact provider anchor tuples\n   `{currentAnchorDigest,epoch,objectId}`, never AHE `PresentHead` locators.\n   Without live activation, the operation authenticates the pending-selected\n   complete candidate from pinned genesis and prior trust. If the AHE is old it\n   completes the exact head CAS; if the AHE is already new it proves that the\n   authenticated successor trust equals `expectedNextRoomHead`; generation ID\n   is irrelevant in this already-new case. Exact success keys are\n   `{head,lifecycle,ok,recovery}` with\n   `lifecycle:\"successor-published\"` and `recovery:\"active-new\"`; failure keys\n   remain `{detail,kind,ok}`. AHE generation ID, revision, and closure digest are\n   locators resolved inside Node only after candidate authentication.\n3. Recovery selection explicitly handles retry leftovers. Among fully\n   authenticated Complete candidates whose previous/current trust equals\n   `expectedPreviousRoomHead` and whose successor anchor equals\n   `expectedNextRoomHead`, candidates with one identical authenticated closure\n   digest are equivalent; while AHE is still old, recovery deterministically\n   selects the lexicographically smallest exact encoded generation-ID string\n   and leaves the others unselected. D.110c-0b0/0b1 owns reclamation and\n   durable-census accounting for those inert equivalent leftovers; 0b0a proves\n   only that they cannot affect authentication.\n   An extra Staged/incomplete/unmatched generation has no authority. No matching\n   Complete candidate, malformed/foreign state, or two authenticated matching\n   candidates with different closure digests is a fail-closed missing,\n   invalid, or true-fork result. This covers a stage crash before provider\n   pending followed by a successful retry that leaves two content-identical\n   Complete generations.\n4. The existing `commitCreatorSuccessorAdoption` module, exact export roster,\n   input/result shapes, direct-call semantics, and current product use remain\n   unchanged during 0b0a. Its documentation records that the retained one-call\n   API supplies no freshness publication and must not be used to advance a provider-scoped\n   product room. D.110c-0b0, not 0b0a, later rewrites the product to the frozen\n   stage → provider begin-CAS → Node publish → provider commit-CAS → exact\n   dual-owner reread → activation sequence and updates the two retained\n   source-governance contracts that currently require the one-call product\n   owner.\n5. D.110c-0b0 also retains its already accepted activation gate: hot activation\n   receives the copied exact new stable room-head tuple, Node requires it to\n   equal the published successor trust, and the trusted product obtains/passes\n   it only after provider commit and exact stable reread. The 0b0 negative gate\n   must prove that a still-pending/old provider prevents any activation call or\n   live successor owner. The 0b0a publish capability alone is not freshness\n   authority and 0b0a makes no product-activation claim.\n\nThis additive Node lifecycle surface is a high-risk public-contract exception.\nOne bounded Grok 4.6/high, direct Kimi K3 100-step, and Opus xhigh plan review\nmust inspect the exact API/ownership design before RED. Only P0/P1 blocks; one\nconfirmation is permitted only if a correction changes executable semantics,\nscope, or the public contract. Deterministic RED then replaces prose inference:\none genuine first-transition fixture must prove that the current public API has\nno durable-complete/no-head-swap capability and no non-activating pending cold\nrecovery owner, failing with exact token\n`D110C_0B0A_STAGED_HANDOFF_SEAM_MISSING`. RED must not alter product source or\nrun a retained campaign.\n\nGREEN acceptance is exact and Node-only:\n\n- after genuine stage, the candidate is complete and fully authenticated, the\n  AHE head remains the prior exact head, no provider call has occurred, and no\n  successor owner has activated;\n- publish refuses a missing, foreign, replayed, duplicated, already-consumed,\n  cross-handle, wrong-head, or mutated staged capability and preserves exact\n  existing failure custody;\n- publish performs one exact head CAS and resolves an ambiguous result by\n  authenticated equality, never by assuming success;\n- cold pending recovery covers both provider/AHE orderings, candidate absent,\n  candidate incomplete, wrong previous/next provider anchor tuple, equivalent\n  duplicate Complete candidates, different-closure true fork, malformed\n  stores, abandoned pre-pending candidate, and ambiguous CAS, without\n  activation and without deriving either expected tuple from room storage;\n- a tests-only deterministic decision model composes stage, a modeled pending\n  boundary, publish, a modeled stable boundary, and recovery to prove that the\n  Node calls support the frozen six-step order. It does not add the provider\n  public contract, rewrite the product, or claim the complete 0b0 crash matrix;\n- the old one-call API, exact module export roster, and retained product-owner\n  source predicates keep their previously proved semantics; adding the two new\n  non-root subpaths updates only the exact package-export-map snapshots that\n  enumerate every `@ts-drp/node` export;\n- no provider object crosses into Node or protocol-v3, and no wire record,\n  schema, digest, authority, dependency, threshold, rollback generation,\n  availability rule, or public product capability beyond the reviewed Node\n  lifecycle seam changes; and\n- exact-owner source-shape tests, Node builds/typechecks, focused genuine\n  runtime tests, all retained creator adoption/activation/reopen and cleanup\n  tests, lint/format/diff, protected paths, stashes, signed commits, pushed refs,\n  and self-excluding evidence manifests pass. Product/example browser controls\n  remain unchanged and are rerun by 0b0 after its product rewrite.\n\nAfter signed/pushed GREEN, one formal Grok/Kimi/Opus review covers plan → RED →\nGREEN causality, the additive compatibility boundary, capability custody,\nnon-activating recovery, and retained behavior. Only then may 0b0 resume and\nimplement provider initialization, product orchestration, expected-head\nactivation/reopen gates, classification, the full crash matrix, the authorized\nsource-governance updates, and the already frozen focused/retained gates.\nD.110c-0b0a does not implement the freshness provider, rewrite the product,\nchange existing creator-adoption-commit contracts, add the bounded checkpoint\nopener, perform repeated rollover or pruning, evolve the archive, or run any\nlong campaign.\n\nThe first D.110c-0b0a plan review inspected signed/pushed commit\n`7f6d05d366466a7e1c5e0a6e37d5bb1f8cab1e29` in a clean detached checkout.\nPrompt SHA-256 is\n`64a777daf5218d89cc28e13aba6886bac1adb52a831337de1969042170665eb5`.\nGrok 4.6/high completed with `stop_reason=end_turn` after active inspection but\nplaced explanatory prose before its terminal JSON, so the runner honestly\nclassified it `NO_VERDICT`; its public terminal content was `BLOCKED` with two\nP1 and one P2. Grok event/public/status SHA-256 values are\n`3907660e807de0d48f77d6914546df71d4e5cf40f84f01ae91455e8ffcd4575f`,\n`d2b071cb505bf9d3937a9591af32c1b472536de3db01d8894f6e99aca99d5d8e`, and\n`1b712e1a8bdcc02a943e6d5589b92503e960fb5acdd6c48eac6730f1f8fa9102`.\nDirect Kimi K3 with the exact 100-step control, session\n`session_9e4333d2-a1bb-496c-b489-0b92b51b3dc7`, returned `PASS`, P0=0/P1=0/P2=2;\nits exported-session SHA-256 is\n`63a76d4f0c54a985e138e5f9fcd4831b40c808dd985890bc4444a09e58abc90a`.\nOpus xhigh session `2cfa1f8e-7271-4643-b892-b434a54ca752` returned `BLOCKED`,\nP0=0/P1=3/P2=2; terminal SHA-256 is\n`3e7a818b46b9c65de2c967bc92c0a498f47b63eebcfaae70fe9f6ae941d3c231`.\n\nThe blocking union is accepted and corrected in one batch. D.110c-0b0a is\nNode-only and uses new subpaths so the existing commit export and retained\nproduct-source contracts remain unchanged. It freezes exact operation and\ninput/result names, treats same-tuple/same-closure retry leftovers as equivalent\nwith deterministic generation selection, treats different-closure matches as a\ntrue fork, and explicitly leaves product/provider orchestration and hot/cold\nexpected-head activation gates to 0b0. The P2 union is dispositioned in the\nsame correction: provider tuples are distinguished from AHE locators; the\ncompatibility wrapper is documented as non-freshness; and 0b0 owns the\nsource-governance rewrite. Because these corrections change executable scope\nand the public Node boundary, the single permitted Grok/Kimi/Opus confirmation\nmust inspect the signed correction. No later prose-only round is permitted.\n\nThe single confirmation inspected signed/pushed correction\n`4f893654e6456ca94384277054ac51fb2df4413d` from a clean detached checkout.\nPrompt SHA-256 is\n`8ee96fd63c82be173f4b887f5937d0e19b5268d0791e472f84d6d0f9cbfcf96a`.\nGrok 4.6/high completed with `stop_reason=end_turn` and emitted an explicit\n`PASS`, P0=0/P1=0/P2=2 JSON after inspection prose; because the prose preceded\nthe terminal object, the strict runner honestly classified the invocation\n`NO_VERDICT`. It did not cancel, time out, or report a blocking finding. Grok\nevent/public/status SHA-256 values are\n`d5417ff1c8d47d8a9a69f47c7d70043411f4647c4a241e2a0496bfe17d39d5f0`,\n`c74436f74b5994ef8e00456d840c938005613ea5fe5aea3d29bf7