AddressBook the source address book\n263\t     * @param targetAddressBook the target address book\n264\t     * @param targetHintsVerificationKey the hinTS verification key for the target address book\n265\t     * @param aggregatedSignature an aggregated signature from the target address book\n266\t     * @param signers the set of signers contributing to the aggregated signature\n267\t     * @return the incremental WRAPS proof\n268\t     */\n269\t    Proof constructIncrementalWrapsProof(\n270\t            @NonNull byte[] genesisAddressBookHash,\n271\t            @NonNull byte[] sourceProof,\n272\t            @NonNull AddressBook sourceAddressBook,\n273\t            @NonNull AddressBook targetAddressBook,\n274\t            @NonNull byte[] targetHintsVerificationKey,\n275\t            @NonNull byte[] aggregatedSignature,\n276\t            @NonNull Set<Long> signers);\n277\t\n278\t    /**\n279\t     * Returns whether the library is ready to construct WRAPS proofs; that is, whether the proving key\n280\t     * artifacts installed in {@code TSS_LIB_WRAPS_ARTIFACTS_PATH} are complete and verified against the\n281\t     * given archive hash. Callers must pass {@code tss.wrapsProvingKeyHash} from the configuration the\n282\t     * current construction is running under, so that readiness is judged against the same proving key\n283\t     * the network agreed on.\n284\t     *\n285\t     * @param expectedProvingKeyHashHex the expected proving key archive hash, as bare hex\n286\t     * @return whether recursive proof construction may safely map the installed artifacts\n287\t     */\n288\t    boolean wrapsProverReady(@NonNull String expectedProvingKeyHashHex);\n289\t\n290\t    /**\n291\t     * Verifies whether a compressed proof establishes the given metadata in the chain of trust of the given ledger id.\n292\t     * @param compressedProof the compressed proof\n293\t     * @param ledgerId the ledger id\n294\t     * @param metadata the metadata\n295\t     * @return if the proof is 